{title: 633 - When We All Get to Heaven}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #633 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 633}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Sing the wondrous [F7]love of [Bb]Jesus, Sing His [Adim]mercy [F7]and His grace;
[F7]In the mansions [Dm/F]bright and [Bb]blessed He'll prepare for us a place.
[Eb/Bb]When we [Gm]all get to heaven, [Bb]What [Gm]a day of [F]rejoicing [Bb/F]that [Dm]will be!
[Bb/F]When [Gm]we all [Bb]see Jesus, [F]We'll [Gm]sing and shout the victory!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Adim]When we all [F]get to heaven,
[Bb]What a [Bb7/Ab]day of [Gm]rejoicing that will be!
[Bb]When we [Cm]all see Jesus,
[Bb]We'll sing and shout the victory!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]While we [F7]walk [Bb]the pilgrim [F7]pathway,
[F7]Clouds will [Dm/F]overspread [Bb/F]the sky;
[Eb/Bb]But [Gm]when traveling days [F]are [Bb/F]over,
[Bb/F]Not [Gm]a [Bb/F]shadow, [Gm]not a sigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Let us [F7]then [Bb]be true [Adim]and [F7]faithful,
[F7]Trusting, serving [Bb]every day;
[Eb/Bb]Just [Gm]one glimpse [Bb]of [Gm]him [F]in glory
[Bb/F]Will [Gm]the [Bb/F]toils [F]of [Gm]life repay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]Onward [F7]to [Bb]the prize [Adim]before [F7]us!
[F7]Soon his [Dm/F]beauty [Bb/F]we'll behold;
[Eb/Bb]Soon [Gm]the pearly [Bb]gates [F]will [Bb/F]open;
[Bb/F]We [Gm]shall [Bb/F]tread [F]the [Gm]streets of gold.
{end_of_verse}
